# ROOT .dockerignore — the EFFECTIVE ignore file for root-context builds
# (apps/api, apps/worker, migrate, sqs-init all build with `context: .`). Docker
# reads the ignore file from the BUILD CONTEXT root, so per-app .dockerignore
# files do NOT apply to root-context builds — this one does. (apps/web builds
# with context=apps/web, so apps/web/.dockerignore covers that one.)
#
# The API/worker Dockerfiles use selective COPY (not COPY . .), so this is mainly
# a context-transfer optimization + a guardrail against a local .venv (torch!) or
# .env ever leaking into an image.

# Python virtualenvs + caches (a local .venv carries CPU torch — keep it OUT)
.venv/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.uv-cache-local/
.codex-runtime/

# Secrets — never ship into an image
.env
**/.env
!.env.example

# Node / Next build artifacts (web has its own context; keep root clean)
**/node_modules/
**/.next/

# Reference-only material + the original demo
demo/
Prompts/

# VCS, IDE, local data
.git/
.github/
logs/
eval_report.json
chroma_db/

# Docs — but KEEP README.md: the root pyproject's `readme = "README.md"` means
# the image build COPYs it, so excluding it would break `COPY ... README.md`.
docs/
*.md
!README.md
